MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Aenima and Lateralus feel like natural next choices after 10.000 Days because I want more of Tool's heavy riffs, intricate rhythms, and layered songs.",
    "American Idiot and The Young and the Hopeless fit the accessible side of my taste: their energetic guitars and catchy punk hooks connect with my interest in Chuck."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Kid A and X&Y offer atmosphere or melody, but those qualities alone do not satisfy my current desire for heavier guitars and intensity.",
    "The Marshall Mathers and No Strings Attached miss the guitar-driven sound I want, while The Piper at the Gates of Dawn and How to Dismantle An Atomic do not offer the particular heavy or punchy rock appeal drawing me to the other choices."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "Sharing a broad rock connection seems to count too much when psychedelic, gentle, and heavy rock feel quite different to me right now.",
    "The selection feels too broadly centered on familiar albums from a similar period; that connection matters less to me than how the music sounds."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My latest interest in 10.000 Days deserves particular attention because its combination of heaviness and rhythmic complexity makes more Tool especially appealing now.",
    "My listening includes both intense metal and catchy guitar-driven rock, so an accessible choice still needs the energy and punch I enjoy in Chuck."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations partly capture my guitar-driven taste, especially through Tool, but stretch it too broadly beyond the heaviness and energy I want now."
}
